-- Rollback for 0071_autopilot_match_superseded_reason.sql
--
-- Postgres has no `ALTER TYPE ... DROP VALUE`, so the 'superseded'
-- label stays in the type — additive and inert, exactly as 0053 and
-- 0045 left theirs: no reader switches exhaustively on dismiss_reason
-- at the DB boundary, and Activity's review-outcome surfaces allowlist
-- their values explicitly, so older code never sees it.
--
-- The rows the label was written to are deliberately NOT restored.
-- Flipping superseded matches back to (resolution='pending') would put
-- stale suggestions back in front of the user for mail an Active rule
-- has since moved — re-creating the duplicate-action hazard the forward
-- migration exists to remove, and for Unsubscribe that means offering a
-- second irreversible request. A rollback reverts schema; it must not
-- re-arm mail-moving side effects (the 0053 precedent).
SELECT 1;
